@* Open centred band, matching the hero — in this design only the create-a-site form is a floating
   card, so a card here would read as the odd one out. `flex-1` lets the section grow to fill <main>
   (which the layout stretches to the viewport), so the content sits centred with the footer at the
   bottom on a short page. The h1 uses the hero's exact clamp so both titles are the same size. *@
<section class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-center bg-white dark:bg-night-surface">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-6 py-20 text-center sm:py-28">
        @* Positive "it worked" feedback: a check in a soft round badge, using the same glyph as the
           hero's bullet list so it reads as part of the design. *@
        <span class="mx-auto inline-flex h-20 w-20 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-green-100 dark:bg-night-tint">
            <svg class="h-10 w-10 text-green-600" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h1 class="mt-6 text-[clamp(2.5rem,5.5vw,4.25rem)] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.02em] text-green-900 dark:text-night-heading">@T["Your site is on its way."]</h1>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-pretty text-ink-soft dark:text-night-ink-soft">@T["Check your inbox. We've emailed you a link to set your site up, and you'll be exploring the admin in about a minute."]</p>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-ink-soft dark:text-night-ink-soft">@T["The email also has your admin credentials. If it has not arrived, check your spam folder."]</p>
    </div>
</section>
